"""lagrange: the simulator and its viewer from one command, like `gazebo`.

lagrange [SAMPLE | ROBOT [WORLD] | RUN.yaml | PROFILE.yaml] [SERVER OPTIONS] [-- VIEWER OPTIONS]
    the server and the viewer together; closing the viewer stops the server. Your robot starts
    still, on an empty ground unless you name a world, each joint commanded on /joint_commands.
    RUN.yaml says it all in one file (docs/guide/run-file.md); a simulation profile (a YAML
    with domains:) runs as `lagrange run PROFILE` does, with --robot and --world, in the viewer
lagrange --server-only ...      the server alone, headless (like gzserver)
lagrange viewer [VIEWER OPTIONS]  the viewer alone (like gzclient)
lagrange samples                the sample names
lagrange empty                  the ground only; spawn robots into it (like an empty world)
lagrange spawn FILE [--name NAME] [--at X,Y[,Z[,YAW]]]
    adds a robot (URDF, SDFormat, MJCF or USD) to the running simulator, through the
    simulation_interfaces spawn_entity service; the first one in an empty run is the robot
    ROS drives, later ones are passive
lagrange delete NAME            takes a robot out again (delete_entity)
lagrange set NAME=VALUE ...     changes the site while running: gravity (m/s²), wind_speed (m/s),
    wind_from (degrees), temperature (K), air_density, pressure, relative_humidity, rain_rate,
    visibility
lagrange check ROBOT [--overlay FILE]
    what each joint of a robot on the ground must hold against gravity, against its limits
lagrange bake ROBOT.urdf [-o OUT.urdf]
    a new URDF with its concave collision meshes split into convex parts
lagrange foam ROBOT [--speed M_S] [--ground] [--clearance M] [--out DIR]
    the same air through OpenFOAM (GPL-3, a separate program): runs a case, reads its forces
lagrange foam-cht ROBOT --ambient K [--out DIR]
    heat in the links with a thermal material, in still air, through OpenFOAM (RFC 0012)
lagrange tunnel ROBOT [--speed M_S] [--yaw DEG] [--cells N] [--out DIR]
    a wind tunnel: air past the robot, its drag and lift, and a world to look at the flow in
lagrange run|validate|graph|determinism|export|heat|info ...
    the lagrange_server tools (as `ros2 run lagrange_server lagrange ...`); `run` is headless
"""

